course: dictionary
lesson: 13837
title: Jaywalk and staying safe on the road
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Jaywalk is a verb. It means to cross a road carelessly, or in a place where you should not, such as not at a crossing and without waiting for the green signal. «Ben jaywalked across the busy road, weaving between the cars.»
explain: Use context clues to work out the meaning. Busy road and weaving between the cars tell you Ben was not crossing safely. Try the check: swap in «crossed carelessly» and see if the sentence still makes sense. It does, so your meaning is right.
explain: The word changes form: jaywalks, jaywalked, jaywalking. A person who jaywalks is a jaywalker. «The jaywalker stepped out in front of a bus.» Jaywalking is the activity itself: «Jaywalking is dangerous.»
fact: Jaywalk means to cross a road carelessly or in the wrong place.
fact: To cross safely, use a crossing, wait for the green man, and look both ways.
fact: Never jaywalk between parked cars, because drivers may not see you step out.
fact: «Jaywalker» means a person who jaywalks.
fact: In some places, such as parts of the USA and Canada, jaywalking can be against the law.
exercise: «Mia jaywalked across the road without looking.» What does jaywalked mean? | Ran a race with her friends | Waited patiently for the green man | *Crossed a road carelessly, not at a crossing | Looked both ways twice
exercise: What is the safe way to cross a road? | *Use a crossing and wait for the green man | Step out when a bus is coming | Cross quickly while looking at your phone | Dash between two parked cars
exercise: Which word names a person who jaywalks? | jaywalks | *jaywalker | jaywalked | jaywalk
test: «Sam saw the bus coming and jaywalked, but he should have used the crossing.» What does jaywalked mean here? | *Crossed the road in the wrong place | Stopped to tie his shoelace | Walked very slowly along the pavement | Waited for the bus
test: Why should you never jaywalk between parked cars? | It is the only way to reach the shop | It is the quickest way to get across | The parked cars will move out of your way | *Drivers may not see you step out from between them
exam: Tom says jaywalk means to run fast along the pavement. What does jaywalk really mean? | Walking home from school | Running a race on the pavement | *Crossing a road carelessly or in the wrong place | Playing with a ball near the road
